# PRock03 (Plain Rock asylum) on-foot chain (item103e): the natural west-corridor route to the
# `porte_sec` checkpoint, the guard cine, the magnetic card, the checkpoint opener, then the
# canonical `ReachSpec` corridor north of the airlock across the east wing, as far as the hostile
# central ward allows. No teleports, no weapon/item/goal bridges: every step is player input
# through the game's own movement/use chain.
#
# Measured on-foot flow (probe logs `local/reports/item103e-probe*.txt`; report
# `local/reports/item103e-prock03-hostage.md`):
#   t= 0.5..30.5  the west cell-block corridor (Porte33/35/40/42) to the checkpoint (-3840,1720).
#                 On the way the checkpoint detection volume `DetectionVolume7` fires
#                 `gardien_lostpass`, starting the guard `Cine2` sequence, whose action 12 is
#                 `opendoor porte30` (it later parks the guard at PositionInfo22, ~(-3431,3748)).
#   t=33.5..50    walk north from the checkpoint to the `Porte30` doorway. With `Porte30` opened by
#                 the cine the player passes through (the door leaf is collision-less while open).
#   t=55..58      walk north-west to the magnetic card `Hual02MagneticCardPick0` (-3872,3810); the
#                 walk-over pickup puts `Hual02MagneticCard` (Event 'pass') into the inventory.
#   t=66..97      walk back south. The `Porte30` leaf is a `PlayerTriggerToggle` mover: a walk
#                 through it toggles it shut, so the return re-opens it with the player's own
#                 `use` before stepping through, then returns to the checkpoint.
#   t=100..104    the aimed `use MagneticPassTrigger0` (Tag 'pass') matches the carried card through
#                 `XIIIPawn.FindPowerUpItemNameForTrigger` and its OutEvent 'porte_sec' opens the
#                 `TriggerControl` checkpoint `Porte29`.
#   t=108..135    the canonical nav path from PathNode185 south-east: PathNode53, PatrolPoint19,
#                 PathNode52, AttackPoint12, then the west side of the `prsas02` airlock. The
#                 airlock's two `Door2` movers (Porte27/Porte26) are opened with the carried card
#                 on the aimed `use MagneticPassTrigger3` (`XIII.MagneticPassTrigger.Trigger` needs
#                 `MyInteraction.TargetActor == self`), then the player crosses at the open gap
#                 (~y=975, north of the closed Porte27 leaf) onto the east side.
#   t=137..181    the corridor south along x~-2600 (PathNode61, doorpoint18, AttackPoint47,
#                 PatrolPoint26, AttackPoint48, PatrolPoint17, PathNode166) to doorpoint22.
#   t=182..189    the two `PlayerTriggerToggle` alarm doors Porte11/Porte12 (Tag 'PorteAlarme2')
#                 are opened with the player's own `use` and crossed before they auto-close.
#   t=190..209    PathNode171, doorpoint19, PathNode12, PathNode176: the central-south ward. With
#                 the item107 retail door-bump path (`ULevel::MoveActor` -> `IAController.
#                 NotifyBump` -> `XIIIPorte.PlayerTrigger`) the patrolling ward soldier
#                 `BaseSoldier6` opens the ward doors it presses against, so the ward is awake by
#                 the time the player arrives and shoots down the corridor. The route now stops at
#                 the last measured 150-hp waypoint `goto -2159 204` (the measured stop is
#                 (-2138.8,204.2)), east of the `PorteAlarme2` alarm doors and short of the deeper
#                 ward corridor; measured, the player is at 150 hp there over the whole tail.
t=0.50 goto -1246 2604
t=2.50 goto -1476 2543
t=4.00 goto -1680 2464
t=5.00 use Porte33
t=6.00 goto -1857 2527
t=7.50 goto -2106 2563
t=9.00 goto -2228 2552
t=10.50 goto -2339 2530
t=12.00 goto -2539 2582
t=13.50 goto -2592 2597
t=15.00 goto -2728 2656
t=16.00 use Porte35
t=17.00 goto -2909 2590
t=19.00 goto -3296 2388
t=20.00 use Porte40
t=21.00 goto -3357 2216
t=22.50 goto -3456 2157
t=24.00 goto -3652 1984
t=25.00 use Porte42
t=26.00 goto -3468 2051
t=27.50 goto -3764 2043
t=29.00 goto -3790 2016
t=30.50 goto -3840 1720
# item100j: the guard `Cine2` is a `BaseSoldier` whose authored SeeXIII reaction
# (Cine2.CineInit.SeeXIII -> Play -> StartSequence) restarts the cine when the player
# is seen, so a northbound walk before the cine runs `opendoor porte30` pre-empts the
# opener. Hold at the checkpoint (outside the guard cone) until the guard itself opens
# Porte30, then run the chain; the post-wait schedule is shifted back to the absolute
# times of the previous (IAController-only) perception so the ward behaves as recorded.
t=31.00 wait_until event Porte30 PlayerTrigger 40
# north from the checkpoint to the cine-opened Porte30 and through it
t=33.50 goto -3820 1922
t=34.59 goto -3797 2129
t=36.78 goto -3576 2515
t=38.61 goto -3391 2828
t=40.07 goto -3385 3022
t=41.16 goto -3360 3138
t=45.55 goto -3436 3358
t=49.20 goto -3604 3627
t=50.29 goto -3862 3758
t=51.38 goto -3872 3810
# back south: re-open the toggled Porte30 with the player's own use, return to the checkpoint
t=57.22 goto -3862 3758
t=60.14 goto -3436 3358
t=63.06 goto -3360 3138
t=64.53 use Porte30
t=67.44 goto -3379 3138
t=70.37 goto -3391 2828
t=73.28 goto -3576 2515
t=76.20 goto -3797 2129
t=79.85 goto -3840 1720
# read the magnetic card on the checkpoint opener
t=81.80 track MagneticPassTrigger0
t=82.80 use MagneticPassTrigger0
t=83.80 use MagneticPassTrigger0
t=84.80 use MagneticPassTrigger0
t=85.80 use MagneticPassTrigger0
t=86.00 track off
# item100k: Cine0 (CineController25) is `XIDCine.Cine2` with map SightRadius 800 and
# PeripheralVision -0.1 (a 191-degree cone). It looks at the checkpoint from the north-east
# only for ~1.4 s at ~110.4-111.7 and again at 112.3 (measured: (-3696,722)/yaw 266 at
# 105-110, then (-3564,779)/yaw ~332 at 112.3). Sprint immediately after the chain and clear
# the airlock (>800 east) before it turns; the rest of the route stays in the x~-2600
# corridor and the ward, >800 from Cine0. Cine15/Cine12 also see the player but do not wake
# the ward (measured `prock03-expD.log`).
